# design.md section 7 names bugprone-* and cppcoreguidelines-* explicitly.
#
# The disabled checks below are turned off deliberately, not out of
# convenience; each one conflicts with a decision recorded in design.md:
#
#   *-avoid-c-arrays / *-pro-bounds-*
#       The ABI is C99 (design.md section 5.8) and Skia's own interfaces take
#       raw arrays; forbidding them here would only produce wrappers.
#   *-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#       design.md section 5.15.3 mandates plain POD field storage for render
#       objects rather than accessors over a hash map.
#   *-magic-numbers
#       Golden-image scenes and geometry are full of literal coordinates,
#       which is the point of them.
#   cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage
#       6-3's drawgui.h is the ABI: design.md section 5.8 requires it to
#       compile as plain C, so its constants (DG_ERR_*, DG_NODE_TYPE_*, ...)
#       cannot be this check's own remedy - `constexpr` and `enum class` are
#       both C++-only. #define is the correct, idiomatic C mechanism SDL,
#       Vulkan and every other C ABI in existence already uses for exactly
#       this; this check has no C-compatible alternative to suggest, so it is
#       disabled project-wide rather than fought file by file.
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#       Fires on memset()/fprintf() in examples/19_c_client/main.c (6-3's
#       pure C example) and recommends memset_s()/fprintf_s() - the C11
#       Annex K bounds-checking interfaces, which glibc (this project's own
#       target libc, per doc/development.md) does not implement at all. The
#       suggested fix does not compile here, which is a different situation
#       than "unwanted advice" and the reason this one check is disabled
#       rather than its call sites rewritten around it.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include|src|tests|examples)/drawgui.*'
FormatStyle: file
